<figure class="diagram">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 640 210" role="img" aria-label="Cache-aside read path: the app asks the cache first; on a hit it returns the value, on a miss it queries the database and then fills the cache">
    <defs>
      <marker id="ca-a" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 z" class="dg-ah" /></marker>
      <marker id="ca-b" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 z" class="dg-aha" /></marker>
    </defs>
    <rect class="dg-hot" x="10" y="80" width="100" height="50" rx="10" /><text class="dg-hot-t" x="60" y="110" text-anchor="middle">App</text>
    <rect class="dg-node" x="345" y="10" width="130" height="50" rx="10" /><text class="dg-t" x="410" y="40" text-anchor="middle">Cache (Redis)</text>
    <rect class="dg-node" x="345" y="150" width="130" height="50" rx="10" /><text class="dg-t" x="410" y="180" text-anchor="middle">Database</text>

    <line class="dg-e" x1="110" y1="84" x2="343" y2="26" marker-end="url(#ca-a)" />
    <line class="dg-ea" x1="343" y1="52" x2="112" y2="106" marker-end="url(#ca-b)" />
    <line class="dg-e" x1="110" y1="122" x2="343" y2="172" marker-end="url(#ca-a)" />
    <path class="dg-e" d="M112,112 C250,125 410,115 410,62" marker-end="url(#ca-a)" />

    <g><circle class="dg-badge" cx="226" cy="49" r="9" /><text class="dg-bt" x="226" y="53" text-anchor="middle">1</text></g>
    <g><circle class="dg-badge" cx="226" cy="90" r="9" /><text class="dg-bt" x="226" y="94" text-anchor="middle">2</text></g>
    <g><circle class="dg-badge" cx="226" cy="148" r="9" /><text class="dg-bt" x="226" y="152" text-anchor="middle">3</text></g>
    <g><circle class="dg-badge" cx="330" cy="112" r="9" /><text class="dg-bt" x="330" y="116" text-anchor="middle">4</text></g>
    <text class="dg-s" x="500" y="38">hit → step 2</text>
    <text class="dg-s" x="500" y="178">miss → steps 3, 4</text>
  </svg>
  <ol>
    <li><b>Look up</b> the key in the cache.</li>
    <li><b>Hit:</b> return the cached value (fast path).</li>
    <li><b>Miss:</b> query the database.</li>
    <li><b>Fill</b> the cache with the result (with a TTL), then return it.</li>
  </ol>
  <figcaption>On writes: update the database first, then delete the cache key.</figcaption>
</figure>
